claim.claim-text:
17. An apparatus for controlling the flow of articles, comprising: an infeed conveyor driven in a first direction to convey articles therealong in said first direction, and a variable speed outfeed conveyor driven in an opposite direction to convey articles therealong in said opposite direction; said infeed and outfeed conveyors configured in a vertical spiraling arrangement and spaced apart and generally parallel so as to define a space therebetween; a movable transport member disposed generally across and movable along said space, said transport member further comprising a unitary rotatable member drivingly engaged on its circumference simultaneously by drive lugs defined along said infeed and outfeed conveyors so that said rotatable member continuously rotates as either of said infeed and outfeed conveyors move and said transport member travels along said space if a relative speed difference exists between said infeed and outfeed conveyors causing said transport member to travel in the direction of the faster of said infeed and outfeed conveyor; 

 a rotating conveying plate rotatably driven by said rotatable member and having a size so as to extend over at least a portion of said infeed and outfeed conveyors so that articles moving on said infeed conveyor are carried onto said conveying plate and transferred by said conveying plate onto said outfeed conveyor as a function of the rotational speed of said rotatable member; a reduction gear arrangement operably disposed between said rotatable member and said conveying plate so that said conveying plate rotates at a lesser speed than said rotatable member; and a plurality of independent drive motors configured spaced apart along each of said infeed and outfeed conveyors, each of said drive motors having a load-torque curve such that said motors will increase in speed to take up any slack in said conveyors so that articles on said conveyors are prevented from bunching on said conveyors. 18. A system for conveying articles from an upstream delivery station to a downstream receiving station, comprising: a main conveyor disposed to receive articles from said upstream delivery station and to convey said articles to said downstream receiving station; an accumulator device disposed between said receiving and delivery stations, said accumulator further comprising: endless infeed and outfeed conveyors arranged in a spaced apart and parallel configuration so as to define a space therebetween, said infeed conveyor disposed so as to receive articles from said main conveyor, and said outfeed conveyor disposed so as to deliver articles back onto said main conveyor; 

 at least one drive mechanism configured with each of said infeed and outfeed conveyors to move said conveyors in their respective directions; a movable transport member disposed generally across and movable along said space, said transport member further comprising a rotatable member drivingly engaged by said infeed and outfeed conveyors so that said rotatable member continuously rotates as either of said infeed and outfeed conveyors move and said transport member travels along said space if a relative speed difference exists between said infeed and outfeed conveyors causing said transport member to travel in the direction of the faster of said infeed and outfeed conveyor; and a driven article transfer member carried by said transport member and operably disposed between said infeed and outfeed conveyors to transfer articles between said infeed conveyor and said outfeed conveyor as said rotatable member rotates relative to said infeed and outfeed conveyors; said system further comprising condition responsive devices disposed so as to sense the condition of articles on said main conveyor generally in the area of said accumulator, said condition responsive devices generating signals responsive to various conditions of the articles; and a controller operably configured with said condition responsive devices and said infeed and outfeed conveyor drive mechanisms for automatically controlling the speed of either of said infeed and outfeed conveyors based on said signals from said condition responsive devices so as to control the flow or spacing of articles on said main conveyor by controlling the flow of articles through said accumulator.
